{
  "case": "rs_events_default",
  "kind": "rs_events",
  "note": "The SHARED golden fixture for the UCT Relative Strength EVENT columns (plan 2026-11-05 §7.1-7.12; api/services/relative_strength.compute_phase1_columns). 68 hand-designed daily bars (t = 1780272000 + i*86400) plus a `benchmarkBars` sibling, exactly as rs_line_spy carries its second series; `expected` holds every key of relative_strength.PHASE1_COLUMNS (18), aligned to `bars`, null for None. Events are {0, 1, null}: 1 the event, 0 computed-and-did-not-happen, null the warm-up pad OR a bar the gap rule refuses. Dot columns carry the RS VALUE where their event is 1 and null elsewhere (dotNH→rsNH, dotNHbeforePx→rsNHbeforePx, dotNHred→rsNHred, dotNHpartial→rsNHpartial, dotNL→rsNL). ⛔ `kind: rs_events` has NO _CASE_COLUMNS row, for the same structural reason rs_line has none: compute_case carries ONE series and this needs two — a dedicated test reads it in each lane (test_rs_events_*, pytest; rsIndicator.golden.test.js, vitest). params are snake_case per _schema.md and map to resolve_phase1_inputs keys: lookback→lookback, ma_length→maLength, ma_type→maType, price_tolerance_pct→priceTolerance, red_day_pct→redDayThreshold. ⚠️ lookback is 25, not the 10 first proposed: LOOKBACK_RANGE clamps anything below 20 to 20 (a fixture declaring 10 would pin the clamp, not its own params), and 25 > MIN_PARTIAL_LOOKBACK (20) is what lets rsNHpartial fire at all (bars 20-24) instead of being an all-null column. The series contains, by design: a PARTIAL (short-history) RS high that is a TIE (bar 20); a full-window RS new high that is a TIE with the prior 25-bar max (bar 25); an RS new high BEFORE PRICE, benchmark flat (bar 29); a RED benchmark day with the stock UP (green-on-red) that is also an RS high (bar 30: gor=1, rsNHred=1); a BENCHMARK BAR MISSING at bar 31 (t=1782950400 is absent from benchmarkBars) so rsLine has one null in the MIDDLE and every rs-derived column is null there while pxNH (price only) is NOT; the window-with-a-gap rule: rsNH/rsNL/rsNHbeforePx/rsNHred stay null for the 25 bars 32-56 whose window holds the gap, and resume at 57; gor/rog/rsNHred also null at 32 because a benchmark % change needs two consecutive benchmark bars; rsMa SKIPS the gap (bar 32 continues from bar 30's EMA, never restarts); an RS NEW LOW at bars 57-58; crossDown at 10,16,27,33,40,46 and crossUp at 13,17,29,39,45,60. HAND-VERIFIED ROWS (EMA(5): k = 2/(5+1) = 1/3, seed = SMA of the first 5 valid rs, then rsMa[t] = rsMa[t-1] + (rs[t] - rsMa[t-1])/3; the previous rsMa is read from THIS column). BAR 4: C=104, B=100 → rsLine = 104/100 = 1.04; rsMa = SMA(1.00, 1.02, 1.01, 1.03, 1.04) = 5.10/5 = 1.02 (first value; bars 0-3 null); rsAbove: 1.04 ≥ 1.02 → 1; rsNH null (only 4 prior bars < 25), rsNHbeforePx null. BAR 20: C=106, B=100 → rsLine = 1.06; rsMa = 1.043222994615548 + (1.06 − 1.043222994615548)/3 = 1.043222994615548 + 0.005592335128150667 = 1.0488153297436987; rsNH null (20 prior bars < 25); rsNHpartial: max of ALL prior rs[0..19] = 1.06 (bar 8), 1.06 ≥ 1.06 tie → 1, so dotNHpartial = 1.06; rsNHbeforePx null (rsNH null). BAR 25 (the tie): C=107, B=100 → rsLine = 1.07; rsMa = 1.0599511762456688 + (1.07 − 1.0599511762456688)/3 = 1.0599511762456688 + 0.0033496079181104 = 1.0633007841637792; rsNH: window rs[0..24] = C/100 for bars 0-24, max = 1.07 (bar 22), 1.07 ≥ 1.07 → 1 (ties count), dotNH = 1.07; pxNH: max C[0..24] = 107, 107 ≥ 107 × (1 − 0.02) = 104.86 → 1; rsNHbeforePx = rsNH ∧ ¬pxNH = 1 ∧ ¬1 = 0; rsNHpartial null (the full window owns this bar). BAR 29 (before price): C=108.7, B=100 → rsLine = 1.087; rsMa = 1.061547810692402 + (1.087 − 1.061547810692402)/3 = 1.061547810692402 + 0.008484063102532667 = 1.0700318737949347; rsNH: window rs[4..28] max = 1.07 (bars 22, 25; bar 26 = 111/104 = 1.06731, bar 27 = 110/104 = 1.05769, bar 28 = 1.06), 1.087 ≥ 1.07 → 1; pxNH: max C[4..28] = 111 (bar 26), 111 × 0.98 = 108.78, 108.7 ≥ 108.78 is FALSE → 0; rsNHbeforePx = 1 ∧ ¬0 = 1, dotNHbeforePx = 1.087; benchmark 100 → 100 = 0 % → red 0 → rsNHred 0, gor 0. BAR 30 (red-day high, green-on-red): C=109.5, B=99.4 → rsLine = 109.5/99.4 = 1.1016096579476862; rsMa = 1.0700318737949346 + (1.1016096579476862 − 1.0700318737949346)/3 = 1.0700318737949346 + 0.0105259280509172 = 1.0805578018458518; rsNH: window rs[5..29] max = 1.087 (bar 29), 1.10161 ≥ 1.087 → 1; pxNH: max C[5..29] = 111, 109.5 ≥ 108.78 → 1; rsNHbeforePx = 1 ∧ ¬1 = 0; red: (99.4/100 − 1) × 100 = −0.6 ≤ −0.5 → 1; up: 109.5 > 108.7 → 1; gor = red ∧ up = 1; rsNHred = rsNH ∧ red = 1, dotNHred = 1.1016096579476862. BAR 57 (new low, first whole window after the gap): C=96, B=100 → rsLine = 0.96; rsMa = 0.9698417149232937 + (0.96 − 0.9698417149232937)/3 = 0.9698417149232937 − 0.0032805716410979 = 0.9665611432821958; rsNL: window rs[32..56] = {109/99 = 1.10101, then C/100 for bars 33-56}, min = 0.965 (bars 54, 56), 0.96 ≤ 0.965 → 1, dotNL = 0.96; rsNH: 0.96 ≥ max 1.10101? → 0; pxNH: max C[32..56] = 109, 109 × 0.98 = 106.82, 96 → 0; rsNHbeforePx = 0 ∧ ¬0 = 0. The rsMa values above agree with the column to within 2 ulp (the column is the float recursion; the note's are the exact rationals rounded). Written by a one-off script that asserted every claim in this note BEFORE writing a byte; regeneration is banned (_schema.md). | rog re-pinned 2026-11-06 to the mirror rule (plan 7.9): benchmark UP by at least the red-day magnitude AND stock strictly DOWN; the earlier column fired on flat or mildly-down benchmark days and flat stock days.",
